{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130451-fighting-style-knife-throwing","id":1130451,"title":"Fighting Style - Knife Throwing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-17T13:46:44-07:00","id":1130451,"title":"Fighting Style - Knife Throwing","content":"I'm getting ready to start a Demon campaign. One of my players wants to play a demon whose initial cover is that of a circus knife thrower. As to help with this concept I wrote up a fighting style to go along with this. But as I'm not a game developer, I have no idea if what I made is balanced as far as a fighting style goes. But here it is.<br /> <br /> Circus Knife Thrower Style<br /> Prerequisites: Dex-3 Athletics-4<br /> <br /> o | Balance - The first step of mastering any skill is understanding its tools. With this level the user understands the basics of the balance of a throwing knife. For any knife specially made for throwing attacks gain the 9-again quality<br /> <br /> oo | Moving Target - One of the most famous tricks of a knife thrower involves their assistant spinning around on a wheel. As it isn't easy to come by people willing to let you throw knives toward you in the first place, knife throwers need to make sure that they don't kill their assistants. In a combat situation these skills allow you to more easily account for enemy movement. Whenever your opponent takes the dodge action you gain +2 to the attack. In addition any penalty of hitting a moving target is reduced by 2.<br /> <br /> ooo | Bullseye - A knife thrower has unparalled aim when they are able to focus and pick their target. The user of this skill can give up their defense and in return reduce the penalty for any called shots by 3.<br /> <br /> oooo | I never miss - At this level of skill the knife thrower has an almost super human skill at hitting a target. When using the Bullseye ability they may also pay one willpower to gain the rote quality to the roll. (any die that don't come up as successes can be rerolled once)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13933-the-running-halfling","name":"The Running Halfling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13933_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:51:28-07:00","id":1130457,"title":"","content":"I like it, but have Balance do 8-again, 9-again is not worth 1 Merit point.<br /> <br /> Also giving up Defense with a ranged weapon seems a little cheap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:55:44-07:00","id":1130462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130451-fighting-style-knife-throwing?p=1130457#post1130457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, but have Balance do 8-again, 9-again is not worth 1 Merit point.<br /> <br /> Also giving up Defense with a ranged weapon seems a little cheap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. 8-Again would work. But if giving up defense with ranged attack is cheap, what else could I use for a drawback?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13933-the-running-halfling","name":"The Running Halfling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13933_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:16:31-07:00","id":1130474,"title":"","content":"I looked through Hurt Locker for comparable changes. The ranged Fighting Styles there are pretty powerful, you might take a look if you haven't already. A nice 4 dot one might be one that ignores Defense, for instance, allowing you to throw faster than one can dodge. But one drawback is having the range penalties tripled for medium and long distances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:33:12-07:00","id":1130484,"title":"","content":"Okay, so what if instead of the defense penalty, if all distances are halved, trading distance for precision? I think a knife wouldn't have better than 10/20/40 to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13933-the-running-halfling","name":"The Running Halfling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13933_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:36:33-07:00","id":1130487,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Hurt Locker has a throwing style? Can't he use it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:41:47-07:00","id":1130494,"title":"","content":"It does, though it only goes up to 2 dots. And naturally the two dot one lets you inflict the Impaled Tilt at the cost of giving up Defense on called shots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:51:33-07:00","id":1130624,"title":"","content":"I don't (yet) own Hurt Locker. I don't know if such a style is in there or not. With my homebrew style, I want something that favors pure accuracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13933-the-running-halfling","name":"The Running Halfling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13933_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:05:11-07:00","id":1130647,"title":"","content":"There were a lot more dots for thrown weapons in the preview but they didn't make the final draft. It was two takes on the style by different writers, a 3 dot version and a 4. I think the third and fourth dot of the cut version would fit what you're looking for: Dot 3 granted double the normal bonus for aiming: +2/+4/+6 instead of the normal 1/2/3. Dot 4 cut penalties for called shots in half, rounded up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:53:53-07:00","id":1130661,"title":"","content":"Here it is, courtesy of the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/into-the-hurt-locker/\" target=\"_blank\">open development blog</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thrown Weapons (Style, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Tags: Movement (Agile)<br /> Prerequisites: Dexterity 000, Composure 00, Athletics 000<br /> Effects: Your character is trained to rapidly produce small projectile weapons from nowhere and fling them at an opponent with surprising accuracy. Maybe your character is a magician or a festival performer. Perhaps her training is a bit more formal, taking on the structure of a Japanese ryu. You are a dead shot when it comes to all items thrown, be they cards, knives, shurikens, javelins, or tomahawks.<br /> Conceal Weapon (0) \u2013 Your character knows how to hide weapons on her person so that they are easily accessible and at the ready for combat. Your character gains a +2 bonus to Dexterity + Larceny checks to conceal weapons on her person. Any weapon of size 1 that she has concealed on herself can be drawn as a Reflexive action.<br /> Always Ready (00) \u2013 Your character is accustomed to having a weapon in her hands and to not having it remain there very long. As such, you can retain your fast reaction time and be ready to quickly strike again. Reduce the Initiative penalty for all weapons of size 1 by 1.<br /> Time to Take Aim (000) \u2013 When your character has time to take aim with her weapon, she is always on target. Being in the thick of combat isn't always the time to aim, but when it comes to a stage performance and your beautiful assistant has an apple on her head, you can be sure to always hit your mark. Your character doubles bonuses received for aiming with a thrown weapon.<br /> Always on Target (0000) \u2013 Your character can throw weapons with such precision that even hitting the center spade on that Ace of Spades as it is thrown into the air is no problem. This also makes hitting the eye of your opponent just as easy. Divide all penalties for called shots in half, rounding up.<br /> <br /> ALTERNATE Thrown Weapons (Style; \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisites: Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Quick Draw with a thrown weapon Specialty \u2022<br /> Style Tags: Light Melee, Agile<br /> Effect: Knives, darts, throwing stars and tomahawks are all weapons your character can send flying in her enemy's direction. Many warrior cultures have used thrown projectiles in wartime or for hunting purposes and may teach this Style. Also, similar techniques are found among circus and sideshow acts. These maneuvers may only be performed with edged weapons Size 1 or smaller.<br /> Practiced Toss (\u2022): Your character knows how to throw her weapon with a quick and fluid motion. Add her Athletics score to Initiative when using a thrown weapon.<br /> Impalement Arts (\u2022\u2022): A well-placed throw staples an opponent's limbs to the environment. If your character succeeds in damaging a specified target arm, leg or hand with a thrown weapon her opponent cannot move from that position until the Tilt is resolved.<br /> Drawback: The heft needed to make her throw penetrate leaves your character vulnerable. She loses her Defense any turn she uses this maneuver.<br /> Many Blades, One Throw (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Your character throws several projectiles at once at multiple targets. By spending a point of Willpower she can throw a number of weapons equal to her Dexterity with a penalty to each attack equal to the total number thrown. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}